RECORD OF PROCEEDINGS FOR THE GOVERNING BODY
OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE
Office of City Clerk
 July 14, 2014
The Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne met in regular session on this date beginning
at 6:00 p.m. in Council Chambers.  Present were: MAYOR - Richard L. Kaysen; COUNCIL
MEMBERS - Mr. Allen, Mr. Brown, Ms. Broyles, Mr. Cook, Mr. Luna, Dr. Rinne, Mr. Shanor, Mr.
Valdez and Ms. Williams.  Also present:  Carol Intlekofer, City Clerk; Lois Huff, City Treasurer,
and Dan White, City Attorney.  The pledge of allegiance was recited.
Recognition of “Cheyenne Weekend”, being produced by C-SPAN and Charter
Communications, to be aired on Book TV and American History TV in the Fall of 2014.  Ashley
Hill, with the C-SPAN Cities Tour Project, advised a filming crew was in Cheyenne partnering with
Charter Communications to spotlight the community through coverage of various places, activities
and interviews.  She indicated the production would be aired on Book TV and American History TV
channels the weekend of September 6 and 7, 2014, and will also be available on C-SPAN’s website
for future viewing.  Ms. Hill expressed appreciation to the City and Charter Communications for
welcoming them to the community and for their assistance.
Consent Agenda.  (All agenda items listed with the designation of [CA] are considered to be
routine items by the governing body and will be enacted by one motion. There will be no separate
discussion on these items unless a member of the governing body so requests and support by two
other members is received. Any item removed from the Consent Agenda will be considered in its
normal sequence on the agenda.)  Mr. Shanor declared a conflict of interest pertaining to agenda item
#26(b).  Mayor Kaysen advised procedurally that since the item was being introduced on the agenda,
it would be referred to Finance Committee and no action would be taken at the current meeting,
noting declaring a conflict of interest would be appropriate for the July 28 meeting.  Mr. Brown
th
moved to approve Consent Agenda items, seconded by Mr. Cook.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” --
all members of the governing body.
[CA]
Minutes from Regular Meeting of the Governing Body on June 23, 2014.  Motion (per
Consent Agenda) carried.
Mr. Brown and Mr. Valdez each declared a conflict of interest (business interest in vouchers
payable to Ameri-Tech HVAC Services and Radio Stations KRAE-AM and KYOY- FM
respectively) and vacated Council Chambers.  Mr. Luna moved to approve payment of vouchers as
presented, seconded by Mr. Shanor.  Upon inquiry, Matt Ashby, Planning Services Director; Mayor
Kaysen; Rick Parish, Parks and Recreation Director; Rob Geringer, City Engineer; Jim Elias, Public
Works Director, and Lois Huff, City Treasurer, provided information relative to the following
vouchers:  All Traffic Data Services, Inc.; AM Signal, Inc.; Ayers Associates; CPS Distributors;
Express Services, Inc.; Solid Waste Professional of Wyoming, LLC; Wyoming Network, Inc.; PAC
(Firefighters) Fund and Nebraska Child Support Payment Center.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” --
all members of the governing body present in Council Chambers.  Following announcement of the
```

